From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6afe: restart the port when DEVICE_START times out

On the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250) the DisplayPort AFE port (0x6020, HDMI
over DP) often gets no answer to its first DEVICE_START after boot or
after the PCM has been idle. The prepare then fails and the stream the
user started is silent. Afterwards the DSP reports the port as already
started (status 9) but still passes no audio; the next stream, which
stops and starts the port, plays normally.

So when DEVICE_START times out, stop the port and start it again inside
the same prepare instead of failing it. Measured 2026-10-07 through a
USB-C dock and an HDMI capture: accepting the "already started" answer
alone left the stream silent; the stop/start cycle is what makes it play.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-07 22:27:30.028695742 +0900
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-07 23:15:29.903774450 +0900
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@
 #define AFE_API_VERSION_CODEC_DMA_CONFIG	1
 
 #define TIMEOUT_MS 3000
+#define ADSP_EALREADY 0x9
 #define AFE_CMD_RESP_AVAIL	0
 #define AFE_CMD_RESP_NONE	1
 #define AFE_CLK_TOKEN		1024
@@ -1713,6 +1714,29 @@
 	start->port_id = port_id;
 
 	ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		/*
+		 * The DSP sometimes does not answer the first DEVICE_START
+		 * (seen on the HDMI-over-DP port after boot or after the port
+		 * has been idle). It reports the port as started afterwards,
+		 * but no audio comes out of it; a stop/start cycle does make it
+		 * play. Do that cycle here instead of failing the prepare.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(afe->dev, "AFE start for port 0x%x timed out, restarting it\n",
+			 port_id);
+		/* an immediate STOP is refused (EFAILED); the DSP needs a moment */
+		msleep(1000);
+		q6afe_port_stop(port);
+		msleep(200);
+		ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
+		if (ret == -EINVAL && port->result.status == ADSP_EALREADY) {
+			/* second START after a successful STOP still says "already": retry once more */
+			msleep(1000);
+			q6afe_port_stop(port);
+			msleep(200);
+			ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
+		}
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(afe->dev, "AFE enable for port 0x%x failed %d\n",
 			port_id, ret);
